      ],
      "summary": "350.org is a international grassroots organization that <cite id=\"5\">mobilizes global climate action through training and advocacy campaigns</cite>. Founded in 2008, the organization works to challenge systems driving environmental degradation and transition toward renewable energy. In FY2024, 350.org recorded <cite id=\"6\">a total revenue of $19,507,313</cite> to support its global campaigns, which include halting new fossil fuel projects and demanding climate finance reform. The organization maintains strong independent accountability, earning <cite id=\"7\">an overall score of 97.0/100 from Charity Navigator</cite> and holding a Platinum Seal of Transparency from Candid. Operationally, 350.org directs <cite id=\"6\">a program expense ratio of 83.2%</cite> toward its core global initiatives. Financial reserves remain resilient, with <cite id=\"7\">7.2 months of working capital available</cite> to ensure organizational continuity. While its programs cover major regions globally, the organization focuses primarily on systemic advocacy and movement building rather than direct humanitarian aid.",
